  "comments": "<p>This New Zealand definitive dollar coin was first issued in 1999 in BU and Proof sets with the obverse featuring Ian Rank-Broadley's fourth portrait of Queen Elizabeth II. The first coins with the IRB fourth portrait to enter circulation were dated 2000. These coins have been minted at various different Mints over the years. From 2010 The $1 BU &amp; Proof set coins (Except for the Unofficial BU Sets of 2014 &amp; 2015 which were struck at the Royal Mint) were minted at the Royal Dutch Mint and are made from Brass instead of Aluminium-bronze.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>In 2014 no $1 Coin was struck at any Mint.&nbsp;</p>",
